{"type":"message","id":"3d63e490","parentId":"8c95ab6f","timestamp":"2026-05-01T13:12:05.492Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Analyzing Pipeline Requirements**\n\nI'm currently focused on the initial research phase. Reviewing `SOUL.md`, it's clear this pipeline depends heavily on other agents. My plan is to execute the commands precisely, starting with removing the agent directory as per the instructions. This seems to be the first step in setting everything up correctly, ensuring a clean slate.\n\n\n**Planning Initial Execution Steps**\n\nThe first step, as I understand it, is to clear out any existing agent directories and session files to guarantee a fresh start, which is what I'm focused on now. I'm executing the `rm` commands from the instructions to prepare the environment for the news pipeline. Afterward, the `openclaw` command, focused on the researcher agent, will be initiated.\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_1777641125447_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/researcher/sessions/sessions.json"},"thoughtSignature":""}],"api":"google-vertex","provider":"google-vertex","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","usage":{"input":8131,"output":157,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8288,"cost":{"input":0.010163750000000001,"output":0.0015700000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.011733750000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777641111424,"responseId":"mab0aZ3RHvnZmsUP07iIiAc"}}
